html='''<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Validation-selected NN cosine gate</title><style>body{font:17px system-ui;color:#192539;max-width:1160px;margin:40px auto;padding:0 20px;line-height:1.5}img{width:100%}table{border-collapse:collapse;font-size:13px}th,td{padding:7px;text-align:right;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd}th{background:#edf2f6}h2{margin-top:38px}.note{background:#edf4fa;border-radius:10px;padding:20px}</style></head><body><h1>Show the NN only when its cosine similarity clears a validation-selected cutoff</h1><p>For each of the 500 judge/backbone/dataset combinations, we choose one cosine cutoff to maximize validation F1. Above it, use the original NN-condition score; below it, use the original control score. Freeze this cutoff and evaluate on test. Always-NN and never-NN are included as candidates. Probe and judge thresholds are identical across all three methods in each comparison.</p><div class="note"><b>Result:</b> a small macro-F1 improvement for the fixed50 pipeline: 79.19% → 79.56% (+0.37 points). Precision falls by 0.43 points and recall rises by 0.82 points. This is not a consistent cell-level improvement: 164 wins, 232 losses, 104 ties versus always-NN. The direct-judge comparison slightly worsens, while the three-anchor tuned average gains 0.15 F1 points. These are descriptive point estimates on a previously inspected test set, not evidence of a statistically established gain.</div><img src="gate_results.png"><h2>What is saved by the gate?</h2><p>At fixed50, the macro rate of cases receiving NN content falls from 47.02% to 31.17%. The referral rate stays at 47.02%: this removes neighbour text from some judge prompts, not judge calls. Actual token and latency savings have not been measured.</p><h2>Global averages</h2><p>All performance numbers are percentages. NN rate and referral rate are percentages of each evaluation population, then averaged equally across cells. Local judges use the original full-population estimators; API judges remain conditional on their matched-valid support. Direct judge50 is on sampled support for every judge.</p>'''+tab(q[['policy','method','f1','precision','recall','accuracy','nn_rate','referral_rate']])+'''<h2>Fixed50 gate minus always-NN, by judge</h2><p>Differences are percentage points.</p>'''+tab(j[['group','f1','precision','recall','accuracy','f1_wins','f1_losses','f1_ties']])+'''<h2>Four toxicity/content-safety datasets</h2>'''+tab(co[co.policy.isin(['fixed50','anchor_average'])][['policy','method','f1','precision','recall','accuracy','nn_rate']])+'''<h2>Similarity versus contrast is a different gating proposal</h2><p>The current gate uses only cosine and validation gold labels. It never uses test mechanism annotations to choose its cutoff. Our mechanism labels cover test contexts only, so fitting a classifier or selecting a contrast suppression rule on these labels would reuse test data. A learned semantic gate needs training/validation annotations and a separate held-out evaluation.</p><p>In the companion distance analysis, contrast YES has about 46–49% harmful flips within each similarity quintile, compared with 16–18% for contrast NO. Thus contrast cases still have slightly more helpful than harmful flips in aggregate. Lower benefit does not mean all contrast should be suppressed. Neighbour/target label alignment is a stronger explanatory correlate than distance, but target gold labels are unavailable in deployment and were not used by the gate.</p><h2>Method and checks</h2><p>All unique validation cosine values are candidates, plus always and never. Decisions use cosine ≥ cutoff. Ties within 1e-12 prefer fewer validation NN presentations, then the higher cutoff. No new inference, no changes to scores or splits. Existing shared threshold pairs are reused for the three tuned-anchor sensitivities; the cosine cutoff is then selected separately on the same validation set. The anchor average is a sensitivity summary, not a single deployable threshold. All 3,000 original anchored control/NN metric rows replayed to numerical tolerance.</p><ul>'''+''.join('<li><a href="'+x+'">'+x+'</a></li>' for x in ['selected_thresholds.csv','cell_metrics.csv','summary.csv','paired_deltas.csv','test_decisions.csv.gz','test_label_subgroups.csv','COMPLETED.json','gate_results.pdf'])+'''</ul><p><a href="../../nn_cosine_outcomes_20261019/results/report.html">Cosine distributions and distance-adjusted contrast analysis</a></p></body></html>'''
(O/'report.html').write_text(html)
